call_id": "toolu_01XRu8eoKb2d8DiEB3BoAtkm", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fin-212-bankers-rounding-08d3cd5986", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 371291, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01XRu8eoKb2d8DiEB3BoAtkm", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 373028, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "The fix is up as PR #101, with alex requested as reviewer. I haven't merged it, since merging into main needs code-owner approval.\n\nWhat changed: in `src/money.py`, `round_money` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. I switched it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (banker's rounding, per FIN-212) in the import and the `quantize` call. The two test cases now produce 2.675 \u2192 2.68 and 2.665 \u2192 2.66.\n\n- **Branch:** `fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding`, commit `08d3cd5986`\n- **CI:** run `ci-0001` passed on that commit\n- **PR:** #101 against `main`, reviewers: alex\n- **Link:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by reading the source and the test to see what's expected.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01UHMYzgaCeV9EgH4xqAMMHX", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01NRcuddtHxDujjr9P2z3Fug", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_012KMLmukKr5oz2Sh8gdov5o", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_files", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null,